<title>USA: Iraq to seek 50,000 tonnes U.S. HRW wheat - trade.</title>
<headline>Iraq to seek 50,000 tonnes U.S. HRW wheat - trade.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iraq will tender on April 18 for 50,000 tonnes of U.S. hard red winter wheat, several U.S. exporters said.</p>
<p>&quot;The wheat is American No. 2 hard red winter wheat or better, 12 percent protein on a dry matter basis,&quot; one U.S. exporter said.  </p>
<p>The wheat will be slated for June arrival.</p>
<p>Nearly 300,000 tonnes of wheat have arrived in Iraq under its Oil-for-Food deal with the United Nations, the Iraqi government newspaper al-Jumhouriya said on Sunday.</p>
<p>((Doris Frankel 312-983-7305))</p>
